    "text": "To learn about the functions of the tidyverse, we will explore a dataset from the Long Term Ecological Research program Network. This data describes the body size of Fiddler crabs in salt marshes from Florida to Massachusetts during the summer of 2016. You can read more about this data here\nClimate change has caused this species to expand its range northward in response to ocean warming. As a result, we can observe the species following Bergmann’s rule, which predicts that organisms at higher latitudes are larger than those at lower latitudes.\nLet’s start exploring the data using R and RStudio to see if the sampled Fiddler crabs follow this prediction.\n\nExploring the Data\nWe will need to start by installing the packages needed for these evaluations. We can do that with the install.packages() function. This make take a while, but don’t worry, once you’ve install the packages on your computer once, you won’t need to do it again!\n\ninstall.packages(c(\"lterdatasampler\", \"ggplot2\", \"dyplr\"))\n\nNow that our packages are installed, we need to load them into our R session. We can do this using the library() function, as shown below.\n\nlibrary(lterdatasampler)\nlibrary(ggplot2)\nlibrary(dplyr)\n\nNow that we have the packages loaded, we can get at our data. Let’s call it crab_data.\n\ncrab_data &lt;- data(pie_crab)\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\ndate\nlatitude\nsite\nsize\nair_temp\nair_temp_sd\nwater_temp\nwater_temp_sd\nname\n\n\n\n\n2016-07-24\n30.0\nGTM\n12.43\n21.792\n6.391\n24.502\n6.121\nGuana Tolomoto Matanzas NERR\n\n\n2016-07-24\n30.0\nGTM\n14.18\n21.792\n6.391\n24.502\n6.121\nGuana Tolomoto Matanzas NERR\n\n\n2016-07-24\n30.0\nGTM\n14.52\n21.792\n6.391\n24.502\n6.121\nGuana Tolomoto Matanzas NERR\n\n\n2016-07-24\n30.0\nGTM\n12.94\n21.792\n6.391\n24.502\n6.121\nGuana Tolomoto Matanzas NERR\n\n\n2016-07-24\n30.0\nGTM\n12.45\n21.792\n6.391\n24.502\n6.121\nGuana Tolomoto Matanzas NERR\n\n\n2016-07-24\n30.0\nGTM\n12.99\n21.792\n6.391\n24.502\n6.121\nGuana To