    "section": "",
    "text": "This website was created as a project towards the requirements of the Graduate Academic Certificate in Science Communication at McMaster University (2026 - 2027).\nI used Claude Sonnet 5.5 to create a template for the Quarto documents, which I then customized for the specific project. The project itself was inspired by Andrew Heiss’ “Visualizing {dplyr}’s mutate(), summarize(), group_by(), and ungroup() with animations” blog post. The interactivity features were inspired by “Parable of the Polygons” created by Vi Hart and Nicky Case.\nThe data set comes from lterdatasampler, an R package created by the Long Term Ecological Research program (LTER) Network."
